---
import '@fontsource-variable/roboto-serif';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const START = 'mailto:hello@intentionaut.com?subject=FDE%20pilot';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Two Day AI Build Sprint Pilot | Saielle DaSilva"
  description="A 2-day FDE pilot to help teams and organizations bring predictability and observability to their AI systems. £4,050 fixed price."
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">FDE pilot</p>
      <h1>Two Day AI Build Sprint Pilot</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I'm offering a 2-day FDE pilot to help teams and organizations bring
        predictability and observability to their AI systems.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Over the last year, I’ve heard from a lot of folks who are struggling
        with the unexpected and inconsistent behavior of AI models. Things
        regress, quality slips, and they don’t know about it until they hear
        from their users.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’ve been building to fix these exact issues: a framework for applying
        deterministic rules to probabilistic outputs, and pipelines for
        decision provenance and observability.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’ve been using these tools for myself and my clients for months now,
        and I’m so excited to offer them as a 2-day FDE pilot. It works like
        this: I come into your environment, work with your team on a sample of
        your real data, and by the end of day two we compare the new results to
        the prior ones. .
      </p>
      <p>
        £4,050 fixed price. If the idea can't be honestly attempted in two
        days, I'll tell you before we start.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ready to go? Any questions Questions? Drop me a line at
        {' '}<a href={START}>hello@intentionaut.com</a> and let’s make something
        happen.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="prose" aria-labelledby="example-h">
      <h2 id="example-h">A real example</h2>
      <ul class="stat-strip example-stats" aria-label="The engagement in numbers">
        <li>
          <span class="stat-num">3.7 days</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Average time per release, down from 7.7 days</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="stat-num">80%+</span>
          <span class="stat-label">New user adoption on the feature</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="stat-num">Weekly</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Consulting real customers, up from once per quarter</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="stat-num">31%</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Of new features built by one person with only a coding agent had invisible errors, down from 68%</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        One client validated a platform bet for their data stack in 48 hours,
        then worked with me for four weeks. We built a prototype experience in
        two days and showed the concept could work. The longer build took a few
        weeks.
      </p>
      <p>
        They're seeing strong adoption and consistent improvements in data they
        had wanted to act on, which had sat in the backlog for a few months.
        The team has built confidence and does more user research. I taught
        them how to build with AI, getting them to work through issues daily
        and improving their AI native ways of working as a team.
      </p>
      <p>
        Along the way, the team struggled with what AI agents can do and how.
        That showed up as invisible errors from incomplete harnesses and
        deterministic checks.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn-primary" href={START}>Start the FDE pilot</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .example-stats {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .example-stats {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
